from spell_evals_base import s

# ───────────── Ranks 6–9, fuller evaluations (override spell_evals2) ─────────────
s('Chain Lightning', '400000', 'BCD', "Chain Lightning only affects the struck creature when delivered through Spellstrike, so its value for Cyrus is as a normal cast. It can arc through any number of enemies while skipping allies, which makes it safe in a crowded melee. The drawback is that the chain stops as soon as any target critically succeeds, and that happens more often against Cyrus's spell DC than against a full caster's. The Druid's area spells usually cover this role better.")
s('Petrify', '040000', 'BCD', "Petrify slows the target for a round even on a successful save, so it always costs the enemy an action. On a failure, the slowed condition can grow each turn until the target is turned to stone, although those follow-up saves have the incapacitation trait and favour stronger enemies. It is a reasonable Fortitude payload against organic creatures, but Weight of the World is the more dependable choice for slots of this rank.")
s('Cast into Time', '330000', 'CCD', "Cast into Time removes every creature in a 15-foot cone from the battlefield until the end of Cyrus's turn, then they return and take mental and bludgeoning damage. Because they are gone for the rest of his turn, he can't follow up with Strikes or a Trip on them. It fits Aspera's time theme, which is why it is on the stave, but as a combat spell it mainly offers damage against Fortitude.")
s('Unexpected Transposition', '000430', 'BCD', "Unexpected Transposition is a reaction that swaps Cyrus with another creature within 30 feet when he is targeted by a Strike, so the attack resolves against them instead. Swapping with an enemy is the best use, since an unwilling creature gets a Will save but the reward is the enemy taking its own ally's attack. It competes with Reactive Strike for his reaction, so it is best prepared for fights against a single dangerous attacker.")
s('Collective Transposition', '020050', 'BBD', "Collective Transposition teleports two or more creatures to new positions within 30 feet, with unwilling targets attempting a Will save. It can set up flanks, move a caster out of danger, or pull an enemy away from a downed ally. It is a strong tactical tool when positioning is the problem the fight presents.")
s('Truesight', '000005', 'CAC', "Truesight lets Cyrus see through illusions and shapechanging effects within 60 feet for 10 minutes, based on a secret counteract check. It is most useful in court intrigue, infiltration and against creatures that hide their true form, all of which suit the campaign's style. A scroll covers these occasions without spending a slot.")
s('Mislead', '000433', 'BBD', "Mislead makes Cyrus invisible and creates an illusory duplicate that he directs, and the invisibility survives hostile actions. He can make enemies believe the duplicate made his attacks. It suits deception and safe repositioning, but sustaining it costs an action each turn, which conflicts with Spellstrike and recharging.")
s('Teleport', '000005', 'CAC', "Teleport moves Cyrus and up to four others up to 100 miles after a 10-minute cast. It is an expedition and travel tool rather than a combat spell, and a scroll is the sensible way to carry it for the occasional long journey.")
s('Silver Spear', '500000', 'ACD', "Silver Spear deals 12d6 piercing damage on Aspera's attack roll, with an extra 12d6 spirit damage against fiends and a teleportation lock on a critical hit. The spear counts as silver, which exploits the weakness of devils. In a Forgotten Realms campaign with frequent fiendish enemies it is an excellent attack payload; against other enemies it is still a solid damage option.")
s('Wall of Force', '050000', 'ABD', "Wall of Force creates an invisible wall with Hardness 30 and 60 Hit Points for a minute, blocking physical effects and incorporeal creatures. It is one of the strongest ways to split an encounter or protect a retreat. It costs three actions and can't go through Spellstrike, so it is a turn spent on control rather than damage.")
s('Beheading Buzz Saw', '400000', 'BCD', "Beheading Buzz Saw is a 60-foot line dealing slashing and heavy persistent bleed damage, with a chance of decapitation on a critical failure. A successful save means no damage at all, which is a significant risk against Cyrus's spell DC. It is a Sprinting Spellstrike option, but Frigid Flurry is more reliable at this rank.")
s('Eclipse Burst', '400000', 'CCD', "Eclipse Burst is a 60-foot burst of cold and void damage that can blind on a critical failure. It is far too large for Expansive Spellstrike from reach, so it has to be cast normally from a distance. The Druid's area spells usually cover this role.")
s('Comet Charge', '500050', 'ACD', "Comet Charge is a large single-target payload with a choice of four damage types, which makes it a reliable way to hit a known weakness. Through Spellstrike it uses Aspera's attack roll, which is higher than his spell attack, and the flight happens after the Strike resolves, which pulls Cyrus adjacent to the target and gives up his reach advantage. Cast normally it is a strong way to reach an isolated enemy up to 120 feet away without triggering reactions, but it then uses his weaker spell attack. It competes with save spells of the same rank that still do something on a miss, so it is best when the target's AC is clearly its weakest defence.")
s('Defy the Gods', '005000', 'BCD', "Defy the Gods leaves the target drained and stupefied even on a successful save, which weakens both its Fortitude and its spellcasting. Against divine, holy or unholy targets it also grants Cyrus resistance to holy and unholy damage. It is a good choice against enemy priests and divine servants.")
s('Spell Riposte', '000403', 'BCD', "Spell Riposte is a reaction that counteracts a targeted spell aimed at Cyrus and redirects it at its caster. It can't affect area spells. It should be prepared when the party knows it will face a caster who relies on targeted spells.")
s('Contingency', '000403', 'BBC', "Contingency stores a spell of rank 4 or lower that triggers automatically on a condition Cyrus sets, such as Translocate when he falls below a third of his Hit Points. It takes 10 minutes to cast, so it belongs in daily preparations. It is a strong insurance policy for the day's most dangerous fight.")
s('Telekinetic Bombardment', '440000', 'ACD', "Telekinetic Bombardment knocks prone on a failure, stuns on a critical failure and leaves difficult terrain behind. It can be placed anywhere within 500 feet, including as a 30-foot line that doesn't start from Cyrus. Prone targets are off-guard, which sets up Laughing Shadow's damage and the party's melee attacks.")
s('Frigid Flurry', '500050', 'SCD', "Frigid Flurry is one of the best line payloads Cyrus can learn. It damages only foes, so it can be sent through a melee that includes the party, and after the Strike and the damage resolve, the wind carries Cyrus to the far end of the line while he is immune to almost everything. Through Expansive Spellstrike that means he hits a whole file of enemies and ends well away from them; with Sprinting Spellstrike the line follows his path, so he can cut through a group, Strike, and be carried on to the end of the line. The weakness is fire, and the carry ends his position at the line's far end, which can put him out of reach of the next target or away from the party's healer.")
s('True Target', '000600', 'SBC', "True Target costs one action and lets Cyrus and up to three allies roll their first attack against the designated creature twice, ignoring concealment and circumstance penalties. Cyrus can cast it and Spellstrike on the same turn, which makes his payload far more likely to land. Its value depends on initiative: it is best when the party's attackers act before the target.")
s('Arctic Rift', '540000', 'ACD', "Arctic Rift is a 120-foot Fortitude line that slows creatures that fail and encases those that critically fail in ice, immobilising them. It gives Cyrus a Sprinting Spellstrike payload for enemies with strong Reflex and weak Fortitude. Unlike Frigid Flurry it can hit allies, so the line needs some care.")
s('Disappearance', '000656', 'SAC', "Disappearance makes Cyrus invisible to every precise sense for 10 minutes, and the invisibility survives his attacks. Every Strike he makes is against an off-guard target, which turns on Laughing Shadow's increased damage every turn. It is also an outstanding infiltration spell for the party's stealthiest member.")
s('Quandary', '060000', 'ACD', "Quandary has no initial save. The target is removed into a puzzle room until it solves the puzzle with checks against Cyrus's spell DC, which usually takes several rounds. Sustaining it costs one action each turn, which is a small price for taking a boss out of the fight while the party deals with the rest.")
s('Roar of Freedom', '403400', 'ACD', "Roar of Freedom costs one action, damages enemies within 30 feet and grants allies 15 temporary Hit Points. A failed save also frightens and stupefies enemies. Because it is a single action, Cyrus can use it on the same turn as a Spellstrike, making it one of his most action-efficient spells.")
s('Desiccate', '500000', 'BCD', "Desiccate damages any number of living creatures within 500 feet with a basic Fortitude save, and plants and water creatures suffer more. It needs to be cast normally to keep its selectivity, so it serves as a big direct-cast damage spell for open fights.")
s('Uncontrollable Dance', '054000', 'ACD', "Uncontrollable Dance leaves the target off-guard and unable to use reactions for three rounds even on a successful save, and a failure lasts a minute. Off-guard turns on Laughing Shadow's damage for every Strike Cyrus makes against it. It is a touch spell, so Spellstrike delivers it at Aspera's reach, though the incapacitation trait limits it against higher-level enemies.")
s('Falling Sky', '050000', 'ACD', "Falling Sky knocks every creature in its cylinder prone even on a successful save, and flying creatures crash to the ground and take falling damage. A failure also stuns. It has the incapacitation trait, but the success effect alone is strong control against groups and flyers.")
s('Foresight', '000603', 'SAC', "Foresight lasts an hour and lets Cyrus use his reaction to make a priority ally roll twice on a save, or make enemies roll twice and take the worse result on attacks against that ally. With one or two fights a day, one casting covers the most important fight. The Champion, or whoever the boss is likely to target, is the natural recipient.")
s('Remake Physiology', '046030', 'SCD', "Remake Physiology imposes clumsy, drained, enfeebled, stupefied and dazzled conditions and a −20-foot Speed penalty, even for a round on a successful save, and a failure lasts a minute. It weakens every statistic the boss relies on. It is a touch spell, so Spellstrike delivers it at Aspera's reach.")
s('Falling Stars', '520000', 'BCD', "Falling Stars creates four 40-foot bursts within 500 feet, each dealing bludgeoning and energy damage. It is enormous and needs to be cast normally, which makes it a direct-cast option for open battlefields rather than a payload.")
s('Phantasmagoria', '440000', 'BCD', "Phantasmagoria damages any number of creatures with mental damage, confuses those that fail and prevents reactions even on a success. It is party-safe because Cyrus chooses the targets. Mental immunity and his spell DC are its limits.")
s('Dimensional Excision', '500000', 'ACD', "Dimensional Excision deals heavy untyped damage with a basic Will save, without the mental trait, and creatures away from their home plane take a −4 penalty to the save. It is a strong payload against fiends and other extraplanar bosses.")
s('Implosion', '400000', 'BCD', "Implosion deals 75 damage to one target with a basic Fortitude save, then a new target each time it is sustained. The first target can be delivered through Spellstrike, but sustaining it each turn competes with Cyrus's recharge actions.")
s('Massacre', '500000', 'BCD', "Massacre kills creatures of level 17 or lower that fail their Fortitude save in a 60-foot line, and deals heavy damage on a success. If it doesn't kill anything, it backfires on Cyrus. It is a high-risk Sprinting Spellstrike option against groups of weaker enemies.")
s('Disintegrate', '600000', 'ABD', "Disintegrate deals 12d10 untyped damage on Aspera's attack roll, but the target still gets a basic Fortitude save, and a critical hit only worsens that save by one degree. Against a level-14 boss at level 12, with Sure Strike, it averages about 25 spell damage against a moderate Fortitude save, where Blood Feast heightened to rank 6 averages about 37 with no save; it only pulls level against low Fortitude. Its strengths are the ceiling, since a critical hit against a failed save doubles to around 130 damage, enemies whose Fortitude has been lowered by Blister Bomb or Eagle's Cry, and its utility: it destroys a wall of force or a 10-foot cube of matter outright, and a creature it reduces to 0 Hit Points is left as dust.")

# ───────────── Occult only (via Witch or Psychic dedication from level 9) ─────────────
s('Guidance', '000302', 'A--', "Guidance gives an ally a +1 status bonus to one roll for a single action. It is the most useful familiar cantrip because it supports the party's most important check each turn without taking much of Cyrus's action economy.")
s('Forbidding Ward', '000300', 'B--', "Forbidding Ward gives one ally +1 AC and saves against one chosen enemy for a minute. It is a good way to protect a caster or a front-line ally from the boss for two actions at the start of a fight.")
s('Haunting Hymn', '200000', 'C--', "Haunting Hymn is a Fortitude sonic cantrip that can deafen on a critical failure. Frostbite already covers Fortitude, so it adds little.")
s('Wash Your Luck', '000200', 'C--', "Wash Your Luck cancels a misfortune effect on one roll. It is narrow and rarely matters.")
s('Know the Way', '000002', 'C--', "Know the Way helps with navigation and finding a recently visited place. It is pure exploration flavour.")
s('Read the Air', '000002', 'B--', "Read the Air gives a free Society Recall Knowledge about a social situation and a +1 bonus to Make an Impression. It suits Cyrus's court and diplomacy scenes, which makes it a good second familiar cantrip.")
s('Soothe', '000500', 'FAA', "Soothe heals a willing creature at range and grants a bonus against mental effects. It lets Cyrus act as the party's backup healer without taking Yara's actions, and the party has no other occult healing. With one or two fights a day, a wand gives a free heal in nearly every fight, making it one of the best occult purchases.")
s('Bless', '000400', 'FCC', "Bless gives allies a +1 status bonus to attack rolls in an aura. Yara can cast it, so Cyrus only needs a scroll on days it isn't prepared.")
s('Bane', '003000', 'FCD', "Bane gives enemies in an aura a −1 penalty to attacks on a failed save. The Cleric can cast it too, and sustaining it competes with Cyrus's recharge actions.")
s('Sanctuary', '000300', 'FBC', "Sanctuary forces enemies to pass a Will save before attacking the protected creature. It is a useful emergency scroll to protect a downed ally from follow-up attacks.")
s('Protection', '000300', 'FCB', "Protection grants +1 AC and saves, and at rank 3 it also covers allies within 10 feet of the target. A wand provides a daily defensive buff for the start of a fight.")
s('Liberating Command', '000300', 'FBB', "Liberating Command lets a grabbed, immobilised or restrained ally immediately attempt to Escape as a reaction. It costs one action, which makes it a cheap rescue tool.")
s('Ill Omen', '003000', 'FBC', "Ill Omen makes the target roll its next attack or skill check twice and take the worse result. It is a quick way to blunt a boss's big attack.")
s('Lose the Path', '030000', 'FCD', "Lose the Path is a reaction that makes a charging creature treat its movement as difficult terrain. It competes with Reactive Strike.")
s('Phantom Pain', '203000', 'FCD', "Phantom Pain deals mental damage and sickens the target. It is weak at this rank compared with Cyrus's arcane payloads.")
s('Spirit Link', '000300', 'FCB', "Spirit Link transfers Hit Points from Cyrus to an ally over time. It can keep a front-line ally standing through a long fight.")
s('Calm', '040000', 'FBD', "Calm can end hostilities in an area for creatures that fail their save. It is a useful scroll for breaking up a fight the party wants to avoid.")
s('Silence', '000004', 'FAC', "Silence makes one creature soundless, and at rank 4 it creates a 10-foot aura that also blocks verbal spellcasting. It is an excellent infiltration scroll.")
s('Clear Mind', '000300', 'FAC', "Clear Mind counteracts frightened and stupefied, and at rank 4 it also covers confused, controlled and slowed. It is one of the most valuable emergency scrolls Cyrus can carry for the party.")
s('Cleanse Affliction', '000300', 'FBC', "Cleanse Affliction reduces or counteracts a curse, disease or poison. The Cleric shares it, so Cyrus only needs a scroll as backup.")
s('Sure Footing', '000300', 'FBC', "Sure Footing counteracts clumsy, grabbed or paralysed, with more conditions at rank 4. It is a useful backup to Clear Mind.")
s('Paranoia', '030000', 'FCD', "Paranoia turns the target against all other creatures, which is unpredictable and hard to control.")
s('Augury', '000003', 'FCD', "Augury gives a vague good or bad answer about the next 30 minutes. Its information is too limited to be worth much.")
s('Spiritual Armament', '300000', 'FCD', "Spiritual Armament is an attack spell that could be carried on Aspera through Striker's Scroll, but Cyrus has better arcane payloads.")
s('Status', '000002', 'FCC', "Status lets Cyrus track an ally's location and condition until his next preparations.")
s('Heroism', '000500', 'FAB', "Heroism grants +1 to attacks, saves, skills and Perception for 10 minutes. Yara can cast it too, but a scroll or wand from Cyrus frees Yara's slots.")
s('Hypercognition', '000005', 'FAA', "Hypercognition makes six Recall Knowledge checks in a single action. For a Lore-heavy scholar like Cyrus, it is one of the best occult spells to own as a wand.")
s('Defensive Prescience', '000200', 'FCD', "Defensive Prescience protects a familiar from attacks. It only matters if the familiar is in danger.")
s('Begone', '030030', 'FBC', "Begone pushes a creature up to 30 feet with a Fortitude save for one action. It is a cheap way to move an enemy away from an ally.")
s('Strength of Mind', '000300', 'FCC', "Strength of Mind grants a bonus against mental effects and effects that hinder movement. It is narrow.")
s('Focusing Hum', '000002', 'FCD', "Focusing Hum helps stupefied casters and confused creatures. It is too narrow to be worth carrying.")
s('Infectious Melody', '030000', 'FCD', "Infectious Melody hampers enemy communication. It is narrow.")
s('Tortoise and the Hare', '040300', 'FAC', "Tortoise and the Hare slows a foe for a round even on a successful save, and a failure also quickens Cyrus or an ally. It fits Aspera's time theme and is a strong scroll.")
s('Read Omens', '000003', 'FCD', "Read Omens gives a cryptic clue about the coming week. It is flavour more than function.")
s('Honeyed Words', '000003', 'FBC', "Honeyed Words gives +4 to Lie. It is useful for infiltration if Cyrus is the party's talker.")
s('Synesthesia', '060000', 'FAB', "Synesthesia imposes clumsy 3, a Speed penalty, concealment of other creatures and a flat check on every concentrate action, even for a round on a successful save. That shuts down enemy casters and cripples melee brutes. It is planned for Aspera's stave from level 12, where it gives Cyrus a once-a-day answer to a caster or a brute that his own slots can't match. As an occult spell, he can't learn it, so the stave is the only way he can cast it.")
s('Strange Geometry', '040000', 'FCD', "Strange Geometry creates areas of illusory terrain that slow creatures. It takes three actions.")
s('Inevitable Disaster', '400000', 'FBD', "Inevitable Disaster deals 55 damage with a basic Fortitude save after a delay of 1d4 rounds. It is reliable damage against a boss.")
s('Death Ward', '000400', 'FBD', "Death Ward is a legacy spell that grants void resistance and a bonus against death effects. It is valuable in an undead-heavy arc.")
s('Shadow Blast', '400000', 'FCD', "Shadow Blast lets Cyrus choose the damage type and area shape, but the target chooses its save. That makes it unreliable.")
s('Zealous Conviction', '000500', 'FAB', "Zealous Conviction grants 12 temporary Hit Points and a Will bonus to up to ten allies for 10 minutes. It is an excellent pre-fight buff.")
s('Scintillating Safeguard', '000500', 'FBD', "Scintillating Safeguard is a reaction that gives up to five allies resistance against a damaging area effect. It counters enemy blasters.")
s('Spirit Blast', '400000', 'FCD', "Spirit Blast deals heavy spirit damage that can affect incorporeal targets.")
s('Blanket of Stars', '000003', 'FCD', "Blanket of Stars aids stealth at night. It is narrow.")
s('Ethereal Jaunt', '000044', 'FBD', "Ethereal Jaunt lets Cyrus walk through walls for a minute. It is an infiltration and escape tool.")
s('Visions of Danger', '420000', 'FCD', "Visions of Danger creates a damaging illusion area. It takes three actions.")
s('Orb of Twisting Fate', '030000', 'FCD', "Orb of Twisting Fate wastes the target's first action. It is weak at Cyrus's spell DC.")
s('Spirit Song', '430000', 'FCD', "Spirit Song deals spirit damage that reaches incorporeal creatures hiding in walls.")
s('Spiritual Epidemic', '005000', 'FCD', "Spiritual Epidemic inflicts permanent enfeebled and stupefied conditions on a failure. It spreads to casters.")
s('Overwhelming Presence', '050000', 'FCD', "Overwhelming Presence ties up a whole group of enemies paying tribute.")
s('Unfathomable Song', '040000', 'FCD', "Unfathomable Song inflicts sustained random debuffs on up to five targets.")
